<title>ALGERIA: Algeria's election final results - Council.</title>
<headline>Algeria's election final results - Council.</headline>
<dateline>ALGIERS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's Constitutional Council endorsed on Monday the North African country's general election result, confirming President Liamine Zeroual's supporters as the biggest group in the nation's 380-member National Assembly.</p>
<p>According to Algeria's constitution, the poll results have to be approved by the Constitutional Council.</p>
<p>The figures announced by the council are almost identical to those announced on Friday by Interior Minister Mustapha Benmansour.</p>
<p>Here are the figures presented by the council's head, Ahmed Bouchair, at a news conference:</p>
<p>Party				   Voters	    Seats</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>National Democratic Rally	 3,533,434	 155</p>
<p>Movement for Peaceful Society   1,553,154	  69</p>
<p>National Liberation Front	 1,497,285	  64</p>
<p>Nahda				     915,446	  34</p>
<p>Socialist Forces Front		527,848	  19</p>
<p>Rally for Culture and Democracy   442,271	  19</p>
<p>Independents			    459,233	  11</p>
<p>Workers Party (PT)		    194,493	   4</p>
<p>Republican Progressive Party	 65,374	   3</p>
<p>Union for Democracy and Freedoms   51,090	   1</p>
<p>Liberal Social Party		   36,374	   1</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>				  VOTE FIGURES</p>
<p>Eligible voters	   16,767,309</p>
<p>Voters who cast ballots 10,999,139</p>
<p>Vote participation rate 65.60 percent</p>
<p>Abstained		    5,768,170</p>
<p>Spoiled ballots		502,787</p>
</text>
